WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.840
A forklift stops.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.200
Somewhere, a customer needs a part, and doesn't know its number.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.360
If you know what you want, the Parts Store has the full catalogue: fitment, price and stock on every part.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:21.017
Parts Intelligence answers questions about the catalogue from the knowledge graph.

00:00:21.017 --> 00:00:24.100
Every answer shows its graph path, and its source.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.071
Don't know the part?

00:00:27.071 --> 00:00:28.469
Describe the problem.

00:00:28.469 --> 00:00:36.220
The agent identifies the machine and the part, checks fitment and stock, compares fulfilment options, and recommends one.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.313
One step to the cart.

00:00:39.313 --> 00:00:46.080
Checkout walks through delivery, the dealer, availability and fulfilment, before anything is ordered.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:54.810
Once it's placed, the order is tracked step by step: allocation, fulfilment, shipment and delivery.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.436
Or simply ask.

00:00:57.436 --> 00:01:02.792
The Commerce Assistant reads a mistyped word as the catalogue word, and says so.

00:01:02.792 --> 00:01:10.330
It recommends only a part that fits, has an approved source and is in stock, and shows what it rejected, and why.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.041
Warranty is decided by rules, not by the AI.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:21.130
Every check, the installation, the dealer and the evidence sit right beside the verdict.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:29.238
A shipment from Japan is travelling by economy sea: leg one of four, due on the nineteenth of November.

00:01:29.238 --> 00:01:39.814
The recorded air route takes six days instead of ninety-one, at twelve thousand, six hundred and seventy-five euros, against two thousand, eight hundred and thirty-five.

00:01:39.814 --> 00:01:42.800
Every number comes from the route's own record.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.793
Even where nothing has shipped yet, it shows the routes the network records.

00:01:49.793 --> 00:01:56.480
Lagos: five days by air, or thirty-one by sea, labelled as potential routes, never as promises.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:58.863
Find it.

00:01:58.863 --> 00:01:59.547
Buy it.

00:01:59.547 --> 00:02:00.401
Track it.

00:02:00.401 --> 00:02:01.255
Trust it.

00:02:01.255 --> 00:02:04.160
Agentic e-commerce, at Noordveld.
